i['statement']=i['statement'][:start]+r'''and its intrinsic Coxeter generators are the transpositions of successive elements of each equal-character block in their increasing order. These need not be adjacent transpositions of $S_n$: for $(a,b,a)$ with $a\ne b$ the generator is $(1,3)$. Choose a permutation $\sigma$ for which $\eta=\sigma\cdot\chi$ has each equal-character block contiguous, ordered by first occurrence of the distinct characters in $\chi$ and preserving the order within each block. Write $S_\eta$ for the ambient adjacent transpositions within these intervals, and put $S_\chi=\sigma^{-1}S_\eta\sigma$. The intrinsic length on $W_\chi$ is transported from $W_\eta$; it must not be confused with the ambient inversion length $\ell$ on $S_n$. '''+i['statement'][end:]
